  <office:master-styles><style:master-page style:name="Standard" style:page-layout-name="pm1"/></office:master-styles>
  <office:body><office:text><text:p text:style-name="Title">A Short History of the Ferry</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">Each volunteer described the colours of the evening sky over the dunes for the annual report. The archive keeper compared the colours of the evening sky over the dunes with remarkable patience. The night shift recorded the songs sung at the autumn market despite the persistent fog. Every visiting student compared the colours of the evening sky over the dunes despite the persistent fog.<text:note text:id="ftn1" text:note-class="footnote"><text:note-citation>1</text:note-citation><text:note-body><text:p text:style-name="Footnote">A small working group reviewed the amount of rain collected in copper gauges without any modern instruments.</text:p></text:note-body></text:note> The archive keeper estimated the tidal patterns of the northern bay in a careful and orderly way. The survey team described the growth of moss on the old stone walls while the tide was low.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">Every visiting student summarised the colours of the evening sky over the dunes without any modern instruments. A small working group recorded the colours of the evening sky over the dunes while the tide was low. A small working group reviewed the growth of moss on the old stone walls according to the old manual. The night shift catalogued the condition of the wooden pier while the tide was low. A small working group recorded the condition of the wooden pier for the annual report. Each volunteer questioned the height of the hedges along the canal over three consecutive weeks.<text:note text:id="edn1" text:note-class="endnote"><text:note-citation>i</text:note-citation><text:note-body><text:p text:style-name="Endnote">The archive keeper summarised the tidal patterns of the northern bay using only paper notebooks.</text:p></text:note-body></text:note></text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The archive keeper mapped the colours of the evening sky over the dunes with remarkable patience. The lighthouse crew estimated the growth of moss on the old stone walls despite the persistent fog. The fictional cooperative mapped the number of lanterns repaired each winter despite the persistent fog. The archive keeper questioned the songs sung at the autumn market for the annual report.<text:note text:id="ftn2" text:note-class="footnote"><text:note-citation>2</text:note-citation><text:note-body><text:p text:style-name="Footnote">The fictional cooperative catalogued the weight of the fishing nets after each trip for the annual report.</text:p></text:note-body></text:note> The archive keeper compared the colours of the evening sky over the dunes while the tide was low. A small working group catalogued the growth of moss on the old stone walls according to the old manual.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The survey team recorded the songs sung at the autumn market over three consecutive weeks. Every visiting student summarised the routes taken by the ferry during storms using only paper notebooks. The lighthouse crew estimated the routes taken by the ferry during storms without any modern instruments. A small working group measured the weight of the fishing nets after each trip despite the persistent fog. The fictional cooperative catalogued the number of lanterns repaired each winter before the season ended. A small working group estimated the weight of the fishing nets after each trip according to the old manual.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">Each volunteer mapped the colours of the evening sky over the dunes without any modern instruments. The harbour office summarised the growth of moss on the old stone walls while the tide was low. The night shift described the colours of the evening sky over the dunes for the annual report. A small working group recorded the condition of the wooden pier according to the old manual.<text:note text:id="ftn3" text:note-class="footnote"><text:note-citation>3</text:note-citation><text:note-body><text:p text:style-name="Footnote">The lighthouse crew compared the height of the hedges along the canal according to the old manual.</text:p></text:note-body></text:note> A small working group estimated the tidal patterns of the northern bay before the season ended. The harbour office estimated the number of lanterns repaired each winter despite the persistent fog.<text:note text:id="edn2" text:note-class="endnote"><text:note-citation>ii</text:note-citation><text:note-body><text:p text:style-name="Endnote">The Brindlemoor committee measured the height of the hedges along the canal without any modern instruments.</text:p></text:note-body></text:note></text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">Every visiting student compared the routes taken by the ferry during storms before the season ended. The lighthouse crew recorded the songs sung at the autumn market without any modern instruments. The harbour office reviewed the songs sung at the autumn market in a careful and orderly way. The night shift catalogued the songs sung at the autumn market before the season ended. The survey team mapped the tidal patterns of the northern bay according to the old manual. The night shift reviewed the number of lanterns repaired each winter in a careful and orderly way.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">A small working group recorded the number of lanterns repaired each winter in a careful and orderly way. The Brindlemoor committee catalogued the condition of the wooden pier over three consecutive weeks. A small working group reviewed the tidal patterns of the northern bay while the tide was low. Every visiting student recorded the number of lanterns repaired each winter in a careful and orderly way.<text:note text:id="ftn4" text:note-class="footnote"><text:note-citation>4</text:note-citation><text:note-body><text:p text:style-name="Footnote">A small working group questioned the amount of rain collected in copper gauges according to the old manual.</text:p></text:note-body></text:note> Every visiting student described the number of lanterns repaired each winter despite the persistent fog. A small working group estimated the colours of the evening sky over the dunes while the tide was low.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The harbour office described the tidal patterns of the northern bay while the tide was low. The Brindlemoor committee compared the growth of moss on the old stone walls with remarkable patience. The archive keeper estimated the amount of rain collected in copper gauges using only paper notebooks. A small working group catalogued the amount of rain collected in copper gauges while the tide was low. The lighthouse crew measured the number of lanterns repaired each winter without any modern instruments. The lighthouse crew questioned the height of the hedges along the canal without any modern instruments.<text:note text:id="edn3" text:note-class="endnote"><text:note-citation>iii</text:note-citation><text:note-body><text:p text:style-name="Endnote">The night shift measured the height of the hedges along the canal before the season ended.</text:p></text:note-body></text:note></text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">Every visiting student described the growth of moss on the old stone walls over three consecutive weeks. The fictional cooperative questioned the colours of the evening sky over the dunes according to the old manual. The fictional cooperative summarised the weight of the fishing nets after each trip with remarkable patience. The harbour office described the number of lanterns repaired each winter according to the old manual.<text:note text:id="ftn5" text:note-class="footnote"><text:note-citation>5</text:note-citation><text:note-body><text:p text:style-name="Footnote">Every visiting student recorded the songs sung at the autumn market without any modern instruments.</text:p></text:note-body></text:note> The fictional cooperative catalogued the songs sung at the autumn market for the annual report. The Brindlemoor committee measured the height of the hedges along the canal using only paper notebooks.</text:p></office:text></office:body>
</office:document>
